WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.420
In the book of Acts, about 3,000
people are baptised on a single day.

2
00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:07.880
An official on a desert
road sees some water,

3
00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:10.460
and is baptised there and then.

4
00:00:10.510 --> 00:00:14.820
Yet later, some churches made
candidates train for up to three years,

5
00:00:14.870 --> 00:00:16.790
and baptised them at cockcrow.

6
00:00:16.840 --> 00:00:18.940
So how did that start?

7
00:00:18.990 --> 00:00:23.240
In this mission, you'll read what
Paul says going under the water means.

8
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:26.740
Then you'll weigh up an argument
that still divides churches:

9
00:00:26.790 --> 00:00:29.710
did the first Christians baptise babies?

10
00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:34.880
Your mission: find out how a quick baptism
in water became years of training and

11
00:00:34.930 --> 00:00:36.210
a dawn ceremony.
